domain CC304_FOCUSED_REVISE:
  description "Resume decision for one safe focused revise candidate through the real local path."

problem P1:
  |
    Decide the smallest authorized implementation that resumes cc304 under accepted
    plan revision 8 without returning to broad three-mode completion, migration
    strictness work, or aggregate-test green status.

evidence E1:
  |
    On 2026-09-16 the owner explicitly requested resumption of cc304. Accepted plan
    revision 8 defines cc304 as one unambiguous appearance revise request through the
    real local API or UI, worker, controlled provider driver, common kernel, character
    adapter, persistence, and owner-visible semantic diff, producing a non-current
    candidate without final acceptance, create, migration, paid provider calls,
    deployment, or policy activation.

evidence E2:
  |
    Current branch codex/compact-psyche-repair-integration and its fetched remote REF
    both resolve to 475ff90a5a7ac42645d2ccdd7f02d9f8f8fda23c with ahead and behind
    counts zero. The matching dirty worktree contains the accepted ADR-0034 selector
    slice and pre-existing revision-scope experiments, which must be preserved.

evidence E3:
  |
    backend/src/routes.ts currently starts POST /characters/:id/chat revision attempts
    without a focused source. In contrast, create and migration routes register a
    focused source when the explicitly configured semantic provider exists. Therefore
    the public revision command still falls through to the legacy adjustment path.

evidence E4:
  |
    backend/src/services/character-focused-authoring.ts, character-authoring-jobs.ts,
    the character V3 adapter, durable execution, HTTP provider, review reader, and
    frontend CharacterReviewPage already connect a registered focused run through the
    worker and expose a stored non-activatable semantic candidate review.

evidence E5:
  |
    backend/src/services/character-focused-authoring.test.ts contains a controlled
    loopback HTTP provider and a repository-level revise test, but it does not start
    revise through POST /characters/:id/chat. Under ADR-0034 its existing verification
    REF is source-diverged, so the current file is not valid current evidence until the
    revised exact source is reviewed and sealed against its implementation Causes.

evidence E6:
  |
    The accepted implementation design revision 6 requires routes and workers to call
    the application service, preserves current generation and pointer behavior, and
    makes ready_for_review a stored candidate rather than activation. The cc304 plan
    further limits this slice to appearance revise and controlled local reply.

evidence E7:
  |
    POST /characters/:id/chat is a generic revision command whose existing UI accepts
    changes outside appearance. Treating every request as requestedCluster appearance
    whenever a semantic provider exists would silently change generic product semantics.
    The current compatibility reader also intentionally recognizes ready V2 envelopes,
    not a general V3 authoring cutover. Neither broad change is authorized by cc304.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    Preserve current character revision and pointer. Do not implement final acceptance,
    create, migration, paid provider calls, deployment, Stage identity, policy
    activation, broad recovery, or the unsealed revision-scope experiments.

premise TEST_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Diagnostic execution may reveal implementation facts but cannot establish current
    verification. Only the exact revised test source, with explicit downstream Causes
    to the changed implementation and current governing basis, may become current
    evidence.

pending U1:
  |
    The exact code change remains subject to current-file inspection and type checking;
    any newly exposed contract decision or need to mutate final acceptance must stop
    this slice rather than be inferred.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E6, E7, SCOPE, TEST_AUTHORITY, U1:
  |
    Resume cc304 in the PERT history, then add an explicit local controlled-trial
    buildRoutes option that wires only the selected appearance revision request to a
    frozen current V3 definition and requestedCluster appearance. The ordinary runtime
    build and every request without that option retain the legacy route; do not change
    generic revision semantics or the repository-wide compatibility contract.

decision D2 based_on D1, E4, E5, E6, SCOPE, TEST_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Extend the controlled loopback test so the revise case starts at the real HTTP
    command, traverses the worker and provider, reads the owner-visible review route,
    and proves the current generation pointer and result generation remain unchanged.
    After implementation checks, seal only the exact changed implementation and this
    verification against their applicable current Causes; do not bulk reseal.
